%%abcts what `letter_to_bar` reads past a barline for its ending label: whitespace, an
%%abcts optional `[` absorbed into the barline's own length, then a token of
%%abcts `1234567890-,` — and NOTHING when that token is empty or opens with a `-`,
%%abcts which reverts the `[` too (`abc_parse_music.js:868-887`).
X:1
T:a bracketted ending number
L:1/8
K:C
C2|[1 D2:|[2 E2|]

X:2
T:whitespace before the bracket, which is absorbed with it
L:1/8
K:C
C2| [1 D2|]

X:3
T:a quoted ending label, whose closing bracket is its own barline
L:1/8
K:C
C2|["first"] D2:|["second"] E2|]

X:4
T:an ending with nothing whatever after it
L:1/8
K:C
C2|1

X:5
T:an ending whose measure never closes
L:1/8
K:C
C2|1|

X:6
T:a leading dash is not an ending, and the bracket reverts with it
L:1/8
K:C
C2|[-1 D2|]

X:7
T:a real chord after a barline is not an ending
L:1/8
K:C
C2|[CEG]2|

X:8
T:one ending for several passes
L:1/8
K:C
C2|1,3 D2:|2,4 E2|]
